</section>
<section class="zeroExplain">
    <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">01 &#xB7; The important difference</p>
        <h2>0% down does not always mean $0 to close.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="zeroCards">
        <article>
            <strong>0%</strong>
            <h3>Down payment</h3>
            <p>The loan or assistance may cover the required down payment.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
            <strong>$0?</strong>
            <h3>Cash to close</h3>
            <p>Inspection, appraisal, due diligence, prepaid items, reserves and other costs may still apply.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>
<section class="programCompare" id="compare">
    <p class="eyebrow">02 &#xB7; Six paths to review</p>
    <h2>First identify the program. Then confirm every condition.</h2>
    <div class="programCards">
        <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <small>0% down possible</small>
            <h3>USDA Guaranteed Loan</h3>
            <p>USDA allows approved lenders to finance up to 100% for eligible buyers. The address and income are reviewed separately.</p>
            <div>
                <b>May fit if</b>
                <p>Primary residence at an eligible rural address and household within the applicable income limit.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <b>Confirm</b>
                <p>USDA address, household income, property and approved lender.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="https://www.rd.usda.gov/programs-services/services" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Review official source &#x2192;</a>
        </article>
        <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <small>VA does not require a down payment</small>
            <h3>VA Home Loan</h3>
            <p>VA does not require a down payment and does not require PMI; a lender may still require a down payment in some scenarios and a funding fee may apply.</p>
            <div>
                <b>May fit if</b>
                <p>Veterans, eligible service members and certain surviving spouses.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <b>Confirm</b>
                <p>Certificate of eligibility, entitlement, appraisal, lender and funding fee.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="https://www.benefits.va.gov/homeloans/index.asp" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Review official source &#x2192;</a>
        </article>
        <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <small>No down payment, costs or PMI</small>
            <h3>NACA Purchase Program</h3>
            <p>NACA advertises a mortgage with no down payment, closing costs, fees or mortgage insurance. Funds may still be needed for inspection, prepaid items and reserves.</p>
            <div>
                <b>May fit if</b>
                <p>Buyers willing to complete financial counseling and NACA&#x27;s documented process.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <b>Confirm</b>
                <p>Workshop, membership, occupancy, documents, payment history and minimum funds.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="https://www.naca.com/purchase-product/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Review official source &#x2192;</a>
        </article>
        <article>
            <span>04</span>
            <small>Up to $80,000 in certain cases</small>
            <h3>HouseCharlotte</h3>
            <p>The City publishes deferred and forgivable options for down payment, closing costs and interest-rate buy-down. The maximum depends on the category and eligible assistance that may match.</p>
            <div>
                <b>May fit if</b>
                <p>First-time buyers purchasing inside Charlotte who meet income, price, education and occupancy requirements.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <b>Confirm</b>
                <p>City limits, published maximum price of $365,000, AMI by household, funds and education.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="https://www.charlottenc.gov/Streets-and-Neighborhoods/Housing/Resources-for-Homeowners-Renters/Homeownership" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Review official source &#x2192;</a>
        </article>
        <article>
            <span>05</span>
            <small>Up to 3% assistance</small>
            <h3>NC Home Advantage Mortgage™</h3>
            <p>NCHFA publishes assistance of up to 3% of the loan. It currently indicates a maximum annual income of $158,000 and a credit score of 640&#x2B; for general eligibility.</p>
            <div>
                <b>May fit if</b>
                <p>First-time or repeat buyers purchasing a primary residence in North Carolina through a participating lender.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <b>Confirm</b>
                <p>Income, credit, loan type, price, occupancy within 60 days and participating lender.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="https://www.nchfa.com/home-buyers/buy-home/nc-home-advantage-mortgage" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Review official source &#x2192;</a>
        </article>
        <article>
            <span>06</span>
            <small>$15,000 assistance</small>
            <h3>NC 1st Home Advantage</h3>
            <p>It is a deferred 0% second mortgage, forgiven 20% per year at the end of years 11&#x2013;15. Selling, refinancing or transferring earlier may trigger repayment.</p>
            <div>
                <b>May fit if</b>
                <p>First-time buyers, certain veterans or buyers in targeted census tracts who meet additional requirements.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <b>Confirm</b>
                <p>First-time buyer definition, income, price, 640&#x2B; credit, occupancy and participating lender.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="https://www.nchfa.com/home-buyers/home-buyer-mortgage-products/nc-1st-home-advantage-down-payment" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Review official source &#x2192;</a>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>
<section class="programExample">
    <p class="eyebrow">03 &#xB7; Educational example</p>
    <div>
        <h2>A $350,000 home with 3% equals $10,500 down.</h2>
        <p>Assistance of up to 3% could reduce much of that requirement if the buyer, loan and property qualify. HouseCharlotte or other compatible help could also change closing costs, but the exact combination must be approved by the lender and each program.</p>
        <a class="btn primary" href="/en/qualify">Estimate my starting point</a>
    </div>
    <aside>
        <strong>Important for ITIN buyers</strong>
        <p>ITIN products are a separate conversation. Not every government or state program accepts the same documentation or can be combined. Manuela can organize the questions; the lender confirms the option.</p>
    </aside>
</section>
